Viewer: a performance mode switch for the automatic size (2026-10-23).

On (the default) each window is upsized to the sharpest size (long side 1280 to 1920/2560) and shrunk into
the window: clear, heavier to decode. Off is the normal mode: the window's own size (CSS size times the
pixels used) with a 720 minimum width, so the 2/3 window is 876 wide and the 1/3 720 instead of 490 (its
UI is cramped below that); clarity may drop. Every window size change reconnects; the canvas is never
shared. The Display hint says what each mode does.

